 "arc": "The skate: a side-to-side glide where each push sends one foot out across the floor and the body rides over the other leg. One full cycle, both sides. Frames 0-4 sit over the character-left foot with the character-right knee driving up and out; the arms ride at waist and chest height, countering the legs rather than leading them.\n\nFrame 5 is the first extreme — weight has crossed to the character-right foot, character-left foot off the floor, both arms up at shoulder height and above. Frame 7 passes through the neutral: both feet down, arms dropped low by the hips, the only quiet frame in the cycle. Frames 9-14 mirror the first half onto the character-right support, with frame 13 the matching extreme at shoulder height.\n\nFrame 15 lands back over the character-right foot with both feet down and the arms low, which is where frame 0 picks up — the seam is clean, so the glide runs continuously. Keep the push outward, not upward: the knee lifts only as far as the slide needs.",
